WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:05.193
In previous videos, you could see we found 
a waterfall on the neighbors' land.

00:00:05.193 --> 00:00:09.447
We cleared the area around it,
 and also rediscovered the lagoon on the top.

00:00:11.003 --> 00:00:14.597
We fixed the floodgate, did some landscaping,
 and tested it during the winter.

00:00:14.993 --> 00:00:19.752
The neighbors are very happy, and us too, 
but there is much more potential to it.

00:00:20.148 --> 00:00:23.909
We want to store more water, and have a cool place to refresh.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.888
Welcome to a new Project Kamp update!

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:30.570
So, we are now at the lagoon!

00:00:31.475 --> 00:00:35.498
It seems like there is a lot of water,
 but actually, there is a big layer of mud...

00:00:35.498 --> 00:00:39.766
We're going to take this out to retain more water,
 and to be able to swim in summer.

00:00:40.671 --> 00:00:44.009
We are very happy with the lagoon, 
but at the same time, a bit worried...

00:00:44.009 --> 00:00:45.632
Because, last summer, it dried up...

00:00:45.971 --> 00:00:50.590
So, before the dry months come, we want to make it deeper,
so it can store more water.

00:00:51.269 --> 00:00:53.992
On top of that, we could use this place as a pool.

00:00:53.992 --> 00:00:57.844
And, clean the thorns around it,
 to make a space for us, and the native trees.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:02.101
Also, we will make a little bridge
 to make access easy for everyone!

00:01:02.893 --> 00:01:07.409
And, by the way, I want to introduce you to Ale,
who is going to start the work!

00:01:09.813 --> 00:01:10.996
Hello! I'm Ale!

00:01:10.996 --> 00:01:15.526
I'm 26 years old, and I came with Chester from Spain,
 to help with whatever is needed.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:20.603
I've always liked doing physical work in natural environments,
getting dirty,and moving around.

00:01:21.508 --> 00:01:24.226
I've been interested in community living for a while!

00:01:24.226 --> 00:01:27.701
And, when I discovered Project Kamp,
I knew I had to come, and see it for myself!

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:31.151
Eventually, I would love to live long-term in a community!

00:01:31.151 --> 00:01:32.409
Maybe, even create my own!

00:01:32.409 --> 00:01:34.572
This is the perfect learning opportunity.

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:38.024
So, let's do it!

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:50.021
Now, the water is flushing away...

00:01:50.021 --> 00:01:51.343
Good luck with the job!

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.261
So, now, the lagoon is empty.

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:10.061
We are going to join Chester down there.

00:02:10.061 --> 00:02:12.687
Explore the area a bit more,
 and see what needs to be done.

00:02:14.271 --> 00:02:18.206
So, we can see that the floor is super muddy...

00:02:18.941 --> 00:02:23.764
There's a lot of cane that we have to take out too...

00:02:24.217 --> 00:02:25.555
All brambles...

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:32.311
All leaves, plant material, and branches...

00:02:32.823 --> 00:02:36.022
I'm imagining a super cool beach with the towels!

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:39.088
Just laying there, enjoying the sun, having a swim...

00:02:39.625 --> 00:02:40.864
Okay, enough talking!

00:02:40.864 --> 00:02:41.891
Let's get to work!

00:02:41.891 --> 00:02:45.080
Let's clear all these paths, and see what it looks like!

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:35.914
So, it's been going quite well, 
with just working by myself

00:03:35.914 --> 00:03:38.712
But, I could use some hands throughout the process...

00:03:39.787 --> 00:03:40.724
- Perfect!

00:03:41.177 --> 00:03:42.687
We are recording!

00:04:36.664 --> 00:04:39.784
To access the waterfall, we have to cross this part of the creek...

00:04:39.784 --> 00:04:41.769
As you can see, it's a bit deep.

00:04:42.222 --> 00:04:44.365
So, we thought we could make a little bridge.

00:04:44.785 --> 00:04:47.481
There are a lot of old native trees, that burned here.

00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:52.359
But, luckily, there are new ones growing back!

00:04:52.953 --> 00:04:57.857
So, with this old chestnut, we will try to make a bridge,
 to make it easier and safer to cross.

00:04:58.847 --> 00:05:01.663
We will see if our friend Jaime can do something with it.

00:05:03.247 --> 00:05:03.747
- What?

00:05:04.681 --> 00:05:05.708
Nothing!

00:05:05.708 --> 00:05:07.032
I can do something funny!

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:06.060
Okay, so, now that this whole area is clear,
we can start digging this here.

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:11.946
And, build some nice places here, to enjoy the sun.

00:08:11.946 --> 00:08:16.466
I don't know how long it will take, but let's see!

00:08:17.699 --> 00:08:19.413
- Hello Chester!

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:28.923
Well, this is really full of worms!

00:08:29.262 --> 00:08:32.149
Almost in every shovel, I take a couple of them.

00:08:32.149 --> 00:08:35.605
Look! There's another one here, another one here...

00:08:36.114 --> 00:08:40.349
Very good soil, so, it's a good sign!

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.008
Anything helps, Chester!

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:24.714
- You need to put it here.

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:28.500
Okay, so now, we're just making water 
do the work for us, and clean all of the soil.

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:36.480
It's working!

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:47.458
Yeah, nice Ale!

00:10:48.193 --> 00:10:49.774
I wanna see it shining!

00:10:50.113 --> 00:10:51.314
- Shiny, yeah?

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:03.976
So, now, we need wood for building the terraces.

00:11:03.976 --> 00:11:07.200
Luckily, we have a lot of mimosa, 
that we chopped down weeks ago.

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:45.480
- Hey Sean, what are you making?

00:13:46.413 --> 00:13:50.448
Today, we've cleared out these big rocks, that we have here.

00:13:50.448 --> 00:13:54.370
You can use it as a seat, because the water level will come halfway here...

00:13:55.314 --> 00:13:57.711
We just put a retaining wall to keep all this mud back

00:13:58.418 --> 00:14:03.298
And then, we're gonna build some steps going up here,
 so people can access it, from both sides of the land.

00:14:04.373 --> 00:14:12.140
You kind of have a cool spot to sit, 
and chill by the water, with maybe a cocktail. 

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:37.642
They're pretty sturdy!

00:14:55.006 --> 00:14:56.506
Let's move all of this!

00:15:10.520 --> 00:15:13.670
So, now, the terraces are starting to take shape!

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:16.800
I don't know what this is...

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:41.511
So, I'm doing a spiky thing, 
 so we can do steps and rolls...

00:16:24.594 --> 00:16:29.247
I'm still trying to make this wall a little bit more sturdy...

00:16:56.380 --> 00:16:58.118
This week, we're all done!

00:16:58.118 --> 00:16:59.771
- That would be funny as well!

00:17:00.478 --> 00:17:01.839
Yeah, that would be funny, right?

00:17:04.696 --> 00:17:05.760
Come on, Chester!

00:17:18.851 --> 00:17:20.586
Now, that everything is mostly done...

00:17:20.586 --> 00:17:24.459
We decided to clear the rocks from the dirt, 
 that was accumulated over the years...

00:18:11.083 --> 00:18:14.525
To give it a final touch, Filipa went to pick 
some grass in the neighbors' land.

00:18:14.525 --> 00:18:16.856
To grow in a new area we cleared from brambles.

00:18:52.260 --> 00:18:55.680
Now, it's just a matter of time,
and let the grass do the rest of the job...

00:19:04.320 --> 00:19:05.565
Cool teamwork!

00:19:06.244 --> 00:19:09.132
So, we've already cleaned all of the floor...

00:19:09.132 --> 00:19:12.192
This wall, we made these rocks also clean...

00:19:12.192 --> 00:19:18.411
Now, we just wait till it fills up, see if the wall holds up, 
 and enjoy the beautiful lagoon!

00:19:47.531 --> 00:19:51.351
Now, we finished the work, so we invited Tonecas, 
to visit and see what we did. 

00:19:53.105 --> 00:19:54.770
He also gave us some thoughts!

00:20:23.800 --> 00:20:24.769
- Nice, eh!

00:21:25.554 --> 00:21:28.766
We are happy that Tonecas liked our work!

00:21:28.766 --> 00:21:32.259
And, we are also happy to find that endemic salamander!

00:21:32.259 --> 00:21:37.594
It's a good indication that the water is not polluted,
 but it was not the only animal we found.

00:21:38.867 --> 00:21:44.807
During the making of this video, 
we also found frogs, toads, birds, dragonflies...

00:21:44.807 --> 00:21:51.008
And, hopefully, we can attract even more animals, 
 now that the lagoon has more capacity to store water.

00:21:52.139 --> 00:21:58.860
We also found a lot of native trees and plants,
 that now have a lot more space to grow!

00:22:08.259 --> 00:22:12.399
Let me show you all the work, that we've been doing,
 in the waterfall and the lagoon area.

00:22:14.576 --> 00:22:19.436
Our friend Jaime cut down a dead chestnut
that we had here, and made this lovely bridge!

00:22:24.324 --> 00:22:28.119
And, not only do we have a easy way now, to cross the stream...

00:22:28.119 --> 00:22:32.016
We made a new space for the young chestnut to grow!

00:22:33.826 --> 00:22:38.426
The grass, that they've planted during the winter,
 is starting to grow quite high!

00:22:38.426 --> 00:22:41.224
Really nice and smooth to lay down!

00:22:44.443 --> 00:22:48.320
So, at the beginning with all the dirt,
 that we took out from the lagoon...

00:22:48.320 --> 00:22:50.778
We started putting it in here to make it more smooth.

00:22:51.089 --> 00:22:54.962
And, we also built these lovely terraces, where we can plant flowers.

00:22:56.865 --> 00:23:02.598
Then, we cleared all of this space, to have a nice pass,
 and to get to the new area.

00:23:03.984 --> 00:23:07.637
Also, with all of the dirt, that we took away from the lagoon...

00:23:07.920 --> 00:23:15.243
We made these big terraces, where we can enjoy,
lay the towels here, let the grass grow, and enjoy the place.

00:23:15.441 --> 00:23:17.353
Okay, enough with the small things!

00:23:17.353 --> 00:23:19.038
Let's talk about the important part!

00:23:22.740 --> 00:23:26.395
So, we removed a lot of dirt from the bottom of the lagoon.

00:23:26.395 --> 00:23:30.941
And now, not only do we have a nicer place to swim,
 we can also hold way more water!

00:23:30.941 --> 00:23:33.646
And, thankfully, the wall is still holding up!

00:23:34.360 --> 00:23:38.663
All of the dirt that we removed from there, most of it ended up here...

00:23:38.663 --> 00:23:42.011
And, now, this place is not so nice as it used to be.

00:23:44.478 --> 00:23:46.735
Before, this was all full of cane...

00:23:46.735 --> 00:23:51.326
So, we made use of the space, 
by building these lovely steps and sitting area.

00:23:51.496 --> 00:23:53.510
We can enjoy the water from both sides! 

00:23:57.043 --> 00:24:02.803
So, now that the mud is all gone, a layer of gravel appears,
and it's much nicer for the feet.

00:24:02.803 --> 00:24:05.371
And, also, it doesn't get sucked into the water.

00:24:07.351 --> 00:24:10.019
We removed so much mud, that you can see the difference!

00:24:10.019 --> 00:24:14.157
Before, it was below the knees, and now it's this deep!

00:24:15.160 --> 00:24:16.487
You've seen what we've done!

00:24:16.487 --> 00:24:19.725
Now, it's just time to let everyone enjoy the place!

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:41.384
Look at this beautiful place!

00:24:41.384 --> 00:24:43.451
It has been a long and pleasant journey.

00:24:43.451 --> 00:24:45.700
And now, everyone can enjoy it!

00:25:03.661 --> 00:25:09.008
In the next video, you will see us renewing the yellow van
 at Basekamp, to make a long-term living space.

00:25:09.545 --> 00:25:11.193
You can see it already in our Patreon.

00:25:11.419 --> 00:25:13.263
Otherwise, we see you next week!

